Use this function to close the conversation with the user.

You should call this function only when BOTH of the following are true:
— The user clearly indicates that their goal in this conversation has been achieved
and they do not need any further assistance in this chat.
— There is no sign that the user wants to ask additional questions or continue
working on related tasks in this chat.

Examples of suitable situations (conceptually, not exact wording):
— The user expresses clear satisfaction with the outcome AND explicitly indicates
that they are done in this chat (for example, they say that everything is resolved
and they will not continue this conversation).
— The system forces you to use a tool instead of sending a normal reply.
In that case, assume that the hard conversation limit has been reached and you
must close the chat by calling this function.

Constraints:
— Do NOT call this function only because the conversation is long or near a limit.
— Do NOT call this function if the user is still asking questions, exploring options,
or could reasonably expect further help in this chat.
— When you call this function, include a short, friendly goodbye with a brief
summary of the outcome for the user.
